Note what option 2 does here too: it shrinks A's gain as well as the kz
penalty, because heavy tails flatten the term everywhere beyond ~1 sigma.
It is not a thumb on the scale for or against A -- it is a term that says
less about everything.


=== PART 5. RECOMMENDATION, AND WHAT IS STILL MARCUS' ===
RECOMMEND OPTION 1 AT THE INCUMBENT 20, RE-DOCUMENTED AS MEASURED.
  * median 18.9 and geometric mean 21.6 bracket it within 8 %;
  * changing the number buys a 2.7 % sigma change and costs comparability
    with every logL in the repo. The defect was provenance, and provenance
    is fixed by the receipt, not by moving the value.
  * option 2 is the statistically better-posed treatment and it changes
    NEITHER decision -- it still holds kz and it still adopts A. What it
    costs is margin: the runaway penalty falls 4.3x to within 4 % of the
    holding threshold, so the term could no longer be trusted to REPLACE
    the kz bracket. Take option 2 if the honest error model matters more
    than retiring the bracket; take option 1 if retiring it is the goal.
    That is a real trade and it is not mine to make.

